{
  "title": "Packing station",
  "level": "Foundations · Mixed logic",
  "kind": "pack",
  "brief": "Program the pneumatic pusher at a packing station. It can be operated automatically or manually.",
  "requirements": [
    "Part Present (I0.0) detects a component in position. Auto Mode (I0.1) selects automatic operation. Manual Jog (I0.2) is the operator's manual request. Station Ready (I0.3) shows that the station is available.",
    "In automatic operation, turn Pusher Extend (Q0.0) ON when Part Present (I0.0) AND Auto Mode (I0.1) are both ON.",
    "In manual operation, Manual Jog (I0.2) can turn Pusher Extend (Q0.0) ON even if there is no part or Auto Mode is OFF.",
    "Station Ready (I0.3) must be ON for either type of operation. When Station Ready is OFF, Pusher Extend (Q0.0) must be OFF regardless of the other inputs.",
    "The pusher must be energised only while a valid request exists. When the request disappears, turn it OFF. Do not use latching."
  ],
  "objective": "Combine automatic and manual control with a shared enable condition.",
  "ins": [
    {
      "a": "%I0.0",
      "n": "Part_Present",
      "d": false
    },
    {
      "a": "%I0.1",
      "n": "Auto_Mode",
      "d": false
    },
    {
      "a": "%I0.2",
      "n": "Manual_Jog",
      "d": false
    },
    {
      "a": "%I0.3",
      "n": "Station_Ready",
      "d": true
    }
  ],
  "outs": [
    {
      "a": "%Q0.0",
      "n": "Pusher_Extend",
      "d": false
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Separate the two alternative demands from the common Station Ready condition.",
    "A parallel group can contain two series contacts in one path and one in the other; place Station Ready in a separate series group."
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "name": "Inputs 0 / 0 / 0 / 0",
      "steps": [
        {
          "in": {
            "%I0.0": false,
            "%I0.1": false,
            "%I0.2": false,
            "%I0.3": false
          },
          "ms": 100,
          "expect": {
            "%Q0.0": false
          }
        }
      ]
    },
